    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">Dear colleague,</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">We are pleased to invite you to our next webinar, <strong>Inclusive Elections: Ensuring the Right to Vote for All</strong>, taking place on <strong>Tuesday, 27 October 2026 at 14:00&ndash;15:30 UTC</strong>.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 18px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">The right to vote is written into law almost everywhere, but many voters still find it hard to use. Voters with disabilities, older voters, linguistic minorities, displaced people and rural communities continue to meet barriers at the polling place and in the information they are given beforehand.</p>

    <p style="margin:0 0 24px; color:#333333; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6;">This session looks at what Election Management Bodies (EMBs) can do about that in practice: how polling places are laid out, how voters are informed and how frontline staff are trained, so that every voter can cast a ballot independently and in secret.</p>

